WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.840
Ewan McGregor has gone on the record several
times over the years to say he would be delighted

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:09.660
to reprise his role as Obi-Wan Kenobi if anything
came up, but that he didn't know of anything

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:10.560
on the horizon.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:16.140
As late as 2017, he was quoted as saying he
hadn't met with anyone in any way about a

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:17.179
formal return.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.560
Turns out that was a big fat lie.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:24.160
McGregor successfully bamboozled the public
for a long time, as he's known of a planned

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.580
Obi-Wan Kenobi standalone for four years.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:31.120
He revealed this little fact during an interview
with Men's Journal just before going on-stage

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:34.400
at D23 to make the big announcement of the
Obi-Wan series.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:35.280
According to him:

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.460
"For four years, I've been having to lie to
people about it."

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:42.270
Perhaps this shouldn't come as such a shock,
though, as it's been reported for a couple

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:45.820
of years that Lucasfilm was attempting to
put together a project about Obi-Wan.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.100
Technically, the official reports from legitimate
sources about the project have never said

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:54.160
Lucasfilm was in talks with McGregor, though
rumors have been swirling for months.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:58.780
Of course, he'd at least be aware the project
existed after it got as far as picking up

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:02.640
a director in Extremely Loud &amp; Incredibly
Close filmmaker Stephen Daldry.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:06.900
Until now, it would have been far too much
of a commitment on Lucasfilm's part to announce

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.780
any ties between McGregor and a project like
this.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:14.080
Even if McGregor was only providing advice
to a new Obi-Wan actor, fans would have flipped

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:17.280
their lids even just knowing that he was working
with Lucasfilm at all.

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:20.500
For McGregor to actually star in an Obi-Wan
Kenobi project?

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:25.180
That would have made the Star Wars-loving,
rumor-creating, opinionated public wild, so

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:29.540
it was wise of the studio to keep things quiet
until all the plans were locked in place.

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:32.120
McGregor's secrecy goes deeper than that,
however.

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:36.640
When talking to Coming Soon about the Obi-Wan
Kenobi series' production cycle, McGregor

00:01:36.641 --> 00:01:39.740
revealed that the project was originally pitched
as a single film.

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:40.520
He shared:

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:43.280
"It wasn't always going to be a series, not
initially.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:47.000
When we first started talking about, that
wasn't really in the cards but everything's

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.700
changed so much, so quickly.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:50.760
It's really exciting that it is now.

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:55.000
I'm really into the idea to be able to tell
the story over several hours instead of just

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:55.540
one hit.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.240
I think it's going to be quite cool."

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:01.820
That admission implies that McGregor has been
very aware of the project since well before

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.760
Daldry was attached as director.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:08.660
Daldry has since exited the project, with
The Mandalorian's Deborah Chow now directing

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:09.960
the Disney+ Obi-Wan series.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:12.140
Can you imagine a better comeback story?

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:17.100
McGregor, a longtime Star Wars fan, got the
job of a lifetime in the late 1990s when he

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:20.900
was cast as the younger Obi-Wan Kenobi in
Star Wars: The Phantom Menace.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:25.540
Sadly, the legacy of the Star Wars prequel
films has been lackluster at best.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:29.860
But more than a few fans would argue that
McGregor's role was a rare gem that somewhat

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:30.840
redeemed the trilogy.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:34.900
For him to come back to his career-defining
role now in a solo production where he can

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:37.860
call the shots as an executive producer must
be a joy.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:42.560
From what we understand now, it's clear that
Lucasfilm, Disney, and specifically Kathleen

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:46.320
Kennedy want McGregor's creative thoughts
on display for nostalgia's sake.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:50.160
It's encouraging right out of the gate to
know that the series will have creative input

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:51.700
from the man playing the character.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:56.620
As of this writing, there's no confirmed information
on plot, timeline, or additional characters

00:02:56.620 --> 00:03:00.960
to be featured on the Obi-Wan Kenobi series,
but that almost doesn't matter right now.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:05.840
McGregor is on the cusp of a fandom homecoming,
and Star Wars fans everywhere can take a ton

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:08.600
of solace from the answer to one question
alone:

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:14.820
"Ewan, are you going to be playing Obi-Wan
Kenobi again?"

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:17.660
"Yes."

